labwc-ospite — OUR labwc, only to host the nested KWin >= 6.5
=============================================================

Why: KWin >= 6.5 draws a special black pixel as the root of its window and puts the content in
subsurfaces; wlroots never reports that root as «presented», so KWin gives its clients a clock at 0
and Firefox thinks its window is covered and stops painting.  The fix is a few lines in wlroots
(types/scene/surface.c, in frame_done).  So that we do not depend on the wlroots of each
distribution (0.18 / 0.19 / 0.20, different ABI), we build a labwc 0.9.3 with wlroots 0.19.2
(+ the patch) linked STATICALLY, installed as /usr/lib/remotix/labwc.  src/kwin.c uses it only for
KDE (`make all LABWC=/usr/lib/remotix/labwc`); XFCE and LXQt keep the distribution's labwc.
Details: PIANO.md «Correzione B» and DECISIONI §10.43 (the Alma labwc this replaces).

Files
  VERSIONS    labwc and wlroots, pinned, with sha256
  fetch.sh    fetch.sh DIR           downloads the tarballs into DIR and verifies them
  build.sh    build.sh SRCDIR DESTDIR  extracts, patches, builds, installs usr/lib/remotix/labwc
  wlroots-0.19.2-remotix-presented-root.patch   the patch used here
  patches-upstream/   the same fix for wlroots 0.18, 0.19 and 0.20: for the upstream reports

Built (see the packaging): Ubuntu 26.04 (deb), Fedora 44, Alma 10, Tumbleweed (rpm), Arch.
NOT on Debian 13 and Leap 16 (KWin < 6.5: they work as before).
Licences: labwc GPL-2.0 (corresponding source published with the release), wlroots MIT
(THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES).
